    "methods_description": "Participants (N=30) received laser stimulation at fixed intensities (low pain: 3J or 3.5J; high pain: 3.5J or 4J) in 3 blocks of 10 stimuli each, with high and low pain stimuli evenly distributed. Following each stimulus, participants provided pain intensity ratings on a 0-10 scale (0=no sensation, 4=pain onset, 6=moderate pain, 8=severe pain, 10=unbearable pain). Participants were instructed to maintain fixation on a crosshair display with eyes open, with a 5-second inter-stimulus interval and random 5-second delays between rating and subsequent trial onset.",
